            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of Vinyl-, Allyl-, and 2-Boryl Allylboronates via a Highly Selective Copper-Catalyzed Borylation of Propargylic Alcohols.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6586-6589</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03294</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An efficient methodology for the synthesis of vinyl-, allyl-, and (E)-2-boryl allylboronates from propargylic alcohols via Cu-catalyzed borylation under mild conditions is reported. In the presence of commercially available Cu(OAc)2 or Cu(acac)2 and Xantphos, the reaction affords the desired products in up to 92% yield with a broad substrate scope (43 examples). Isolation of an allenyl boronate as the reaction intermediate suggests that an insertion-elimination-type reaction, followed by borylcupration, is involved in the borylation of propargylic alcohols.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
